> ### Name: brma
> ### Title: Conduct Bayesian Regularized Meta-Analysis
> ### Aliases: brma brma.formula brma.default
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> data("curry")
> df <- curry[c(1:5, 50:55), c("d", "vi", "sex", "age", "donorcode")]
> suppressWarnings({res <- brma(d~., data = df, iter = 10)})
> 
